  "strategy": "1. Approach and rationale:\n\nThe problem requires finding a step function h: [0,2] \u2192 [0,1] that minimizes the maximum overlap integral C5 while satisfying the integral constraint. The previous approach used local search and resolution upsampling but likely gets stuck in local optima. \n\nOur approach applies a manifold optimization strategy that projects the problem into a lower-dimensional manifold of symmetric functions, which is a common technique for optimization on symmetric spaces. We parameterize the function using a reduced set of parameters (e.g., height and width of peak), and then use trust-region optimization to avoid local minima. Key improvements include:\n\n1. Symmetry exploitation: Enforce h(x) = h(2-x) to reduce the problem dimension. This captures the natural symmetry of the problem context.\n2. Functional parameterization: Represent h(x) using basic shape parameters (height, width, vertical shift) rather than direct samples.\n3. Trust-region steps: Use a globally-valid full-space gradient method (TRUST_REGION algorithm) for effective escaping local optima.\n4. Improved evaluation: Use an efficient O(n log n) Fast Fourier Transform (FFT) based overlap kernel calculation that replaces the O(n\u00b2) correlation computation.\n\nThis approach is expected to yield significant improvement over the previous method by leveraging global optimization strategies and reduced-dimensional parameterization.\n\n2. Mathematical specification:\n\nObjective function:\nMinimize C_5 = max_k \u222b\u2080\u00b2 h(x) [1 - h(x+k)] dx\n\nUnder constraints:\n- 0 \u2264 h(x) \u2264 1 for all x \u2208 [0,2]\n- \u222b\u2080\u00b2 h(x) dx = 0.5\n\nDiscretization:\nRepresent h on n grid points: x_i = 2i/n for i=0,...,n-1\n\nOptimization variables:\n- H_0, H_1, H_2: Parameters defining a top-hat (rectangular) base shape\n- Controls over base function: position, width, amplitude\n\nParameters define shape: \nh(x) = \n  H_1 * (H_2 - x) for x \u2208 [H_3, H_3 + t]\n  H_1 * (-H_2 + x) for x \u2208 [H_3 + t, H_4]\n  Plus vertical shift between [0,1]\n\nThe optimization function minimizes the maximum correlation between h(x) and 1-h(x).\n\n3. Implementation procedure:\n\n1. Setup:\n   \u4ece current_parent(280) \u521d\u59cb\u5316, which is the provided parent solution.\n   n_points=560 (target resolution)\n\n2. Parameterization:\n   \u6784\u5efa\u5f62\u72b6\u53c2\u6570\u5411\u91cf: \u03b8 \u2208 \u211d\u2074 (height, width, shift, shoulder)\n\n3. Function from params:\n   \u5b9a\u4e49 step_function_param(theta) that returns:\n     - h(x) = \u5e95\u5c42\u51fd\u6570\n     - \u68af\u5ea6 dh/dx (for gradient-based optimization)\n     - \u79ef\u5206\u4fee\u590d\u51fd\u6570\n\n4. Optimization:\n\u4f7f\u7528 scipy.optimize.minimize with:\n     \u65b9\u6cd5: 'trust-constr'\n     \u68af\u5ea6\u51fd\u6570: \u63d0\u4f9b\u8bbe\u8ba1\u7684\u89e3\u6790\u68af\u5ea6\n     \u7ea6\u675f: \u7b49\u5f0f\u7ea6\u675f (\u79ef\u5206=0.5) \u548c\u8fb9\u754c\u7ea6\u675f\n     \u521d\u59cb\u70b9: \u6765\u81ea parent solution through parameter mapping\n     \u9009\u9879: \u7cbe\u7ec6\u4fe1\u4efb\u533a\u57df\u6c42\u89e3\u5668 (SNOPT)\n\n5. Repair:\n     \u96c6\u6210\u51fd\u6570\u503c\u4fee\u590d\u548c\u68af\u5ea6\u4fee\u590d\u4ee5\u9632\u6570\u503c\u4e0d\u7a33\u5b9a\n\n4. Search choices and useful variations:\n\nThe method uses a single optimization run at the highest resolution (560) but with analytical derivatives. The key search components include:\n\n1. Geometric parameterization to preserve integral constraints\n2. The 1D optimization method allows for easily increasing resolution\n3. Gradient definition has an analytical component, reducing reliable region)\n\n5. Compute budget and robustness:\n\nThe primary time consumption is the FFT-based correlation computation. The trust-region step adds negligible time compared to previous local optimizations. We allocate all 1100 seconds to the optimization with iterative repair.\n\nFalling back to initial values if:\n- Optimization exits with numerical issues\n- Final solution violates constraints\n- \u4e2d\u95f4\u72b6\u6001\u4e0b values exceed bounds\n\n6. Validation and return contract:\n\nOutputs:\n- h_values: Solutions at full resolution\n- c5_bound: Optimized overlap integral\n- n_points: Final resolution\n\nValidation:\n- Check 0 \u2264 h_values[i] \u2264 1\n- Verify integral sum(h) = n/4.0\n- Re-compute C5 using FFT-based cross-correlation\n- Preserve parent solution if fails",
